Relative Xpath:
->path from the current node to the desired element
-> starts with a double slash (//)

-> //taganame[@attribute='value'] or //*[@attribute='value']

-> attribute can be anything that has value to it.
-> example:
For url : https://sqatools.in/automation-practice-page/
To find Automation practice page header:
//h1[@class='entry-title']  or  //*[@class="entry-title"]

######################################################

Single slash: is 1 level down
Double slash between 2 tag is any level down
example:

The below path will give you the hyperlink python basic program
//ul[@class='wp-block-list']/li/a[text()='Python Basic Programs']
and 
//ul[@class='wp-block-list']//a[text()='Python Basic Programs']


But the below will not give the same result coz there is 1 more tag present 
between 'a' tag and 'ul' tag. and single slash means only 1 level down.

//ul[@class='wp-block-list']/a[text()='Python Basic Programs']
